    776  f0c0							; --- VDEL: P0 ON, P1 OFF. NOT the HUD's 13+2 usage — this is the cave's
    777  f0c0							; one-line-ahead discipline, and it is x-INDEPENDENT only when the landing
    778  f0c0							; point of the write is RIGHT of every sprite pixel.
    779  f0c0							; Facts (Stella `Player::grp` / `updatePattern`): without VDEL a GRP write
    780  f0c0							; lands in `myPatternNew` and is rendered immediately, so a mid-line write
    781  f0c0							; affects the CURRENT line when the sprite has not started yet (its pixels
    782  f0c0							; begin at cycle ~(61+X)/3) and the NEXT line otherwise. `myPatternOld`,
    783  f0c0							; the VDEL slot, is latched when the OTHER player is written
    784  f0c0							; (`shufflePatterns`), so VDEL does NOT delay by a line on its own — it
    785  f0c0							; moves the landing point to the other register's store cycle.
    786  f0c0							; Measured store phases (`tools/cycle_ledger.py`, P1 worst path):
    787  f0c0							;   COLUP0 c19 (< all pixels: the per-row colour is always this line),
    788  f0c0							;   GRP0 c35, GRP1 c58, COLUP1 c65.
    789  f0c0							; P0: VDELP0=1 moves its landing from GRP0's c35 (= correct art only for
    790  f0c0							;   X < 44 px) to GRP1's c58 (X < 113 px) and, in the same stroke, aligns
    791  f0c0							;   the art with PlayerColTable (today art row r sits one line above its
    792  f0c0							;   colour for X >= 44). P1 keep VDELP1=0: its latch would be GRP0's c35,
    793  f0c0							;   i.e. a WORSE split than today's c58, and P1's colour would stay at c65.
    794  f0c0							; Every .Line body writes GRP1 exactly once on every path (.Grp1 in-window
    795  f0c0							; or .ObjNoRes blank), so the P0 latch is driven every scanline; that is
    796  f0c0							; the contract `tools/test_vdel_cave.py` guards. HERO clears both bits at
    797  f0c0							; cave entry and uses VDEL only for its HUD text, so this is the one place
    798  f0c0							; we deliberately differ (measured, not guessed).
    799  f0c0		       a9 01		      lda	#1
    800  f0c2		       85 25		      sta	VDELP0
    801  f0c4		       a9 00		      lda	#0
    802  f0c6		       85 26		      sta	VDELP1
    803  f0c8		       85 1f		      sta	ENABL	; HUD-bar leftover off before first visible
    804  f0ca							;   line (.Row row0 BandTab rewrites next)
