   1379  f27e							; --- Clamp fall speed: down at MAX_FALL, up at -$0100. ---
   1380  f27e							; The high byte alone is NOT enough (2026-10-22): `cmp #>MAX_FALL` with vyHi
   1381  f27e							; == $01 is EQUAL, so the old code rewrote vy to exactly $0180 for every speed
   1382  f27e							; in $0100..$017F — a falling player's thrust was computed and then thrown
   1383  f27e							; away every frame (vy: $0180 -> $0188 -> $0158 -> clamped back to $0180), so
   1384  f27e							; the jet could not slow a fall at all. Compare the low byte when the high
   1385  f27e							; bytes match.
