   2608  f7d6							; M1ColFromMeta — A = the async M1 sprite column (M1X) for this room, or 0 when
   2609  f7d6							; the room carries no side-1 patch.
   2610  f7d6							; MetaA ($99, RoomPF0Lo here) = ((m1_col+1) << 4) | band_mask | b3, written
   2611  f7d6							; convert_room.meta_bytes; M1X = 8*col + 7 is that field's inverse. Deriving it
   2612  f7d6							; here (instead of staging at room load) keeps bank3's pinned code untouched,
   2613  f7d6							; and it feeds the hot-overlap box test too, which reads M1X.
   2614  f7d6							; Flags: Z is left SET when A = 0, so the caller can branch right after.
   2615  f7d6							; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   2616  f7d6							; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   2617  f7d6							; DoorLocked — a locked door (M1 patch cell, PF-open) hit by the player.
   2618  f7d6							; In: nothing new (the overlay's box scratch is live). Out: C=1 blocked, or a
   2619  f7d6							; tail jump into HotOverlapFlag when the room is HOT, where the overlap body
   2620  f7d6							; also gets to apply the hot hit.
   2621  f7d6							; Why: the locked case used to jump straight to HotOverlapFlag, and its bank3
   2622  f7d6							; body returns C=0 when the hot stream has no hit — a cold room's door was
   2623  f7d6							; therefore walk-through (user report: "door is not solid, neither with nor
   2624  f7d6							; without the key").
   2625  f7d6							; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
